    "result_text": "The build succeeds and the test passes. The project's only actual test class is `AcceptanceTest` (the other two files are helper base classes).\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level-computation rule with a points system, then derived the level from the points.\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a new read-only `membershipPoints` field to the `OwnerDto` schema and rewrote the `membershipLevel` description to reflect that it's now derived from points (and its example, now `2`).\n\n**`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`**:\n- Added a `@Mapping` for `membershipPoints` alongside `membershipLevel`, so both fields are returned.\n- New `membershipPoints(owner)` method: starts at 0; `+2` email present, `+1` namesakeCount is 0, `+2` for `householdSize >= 3`, `+3` for tenure over 365 days.\n- Rewrote `membershipLevel(owner)` to map points \u2192 level: 1 (0\u20131), 2 (2\u20133), 3 (4\u20135), 4 (6+).\n\nThe `householdSize` field on `Owner` supplies the \"household of 3 or more\" input. This matches the acceptance test: a fresh owner with an email + no namesake, single-member household, zero tenure = 3 points \u2192 level 2.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
