    "probe_text": "Here's the complete ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, which is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:144`). I've grouped it as: what runs *before* the method body (framework), then each step *inside* the method in exact source order.\n\n## Before the method body (framework layer)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role or the request is rejected (403).\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** (`OwnerFieldsDto`, enforced because the generated `OwnersApi` marks the body `@Valid`). Rejects with 400 if violated:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to two space/`'`/`-`-separated parts)\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (as above, optional trailing `.`)\n   - `address`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` (optional): `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`\n   - `postcode` (optional): `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`\n   - `registrationDate` / `birthDate`: `@Valid` (ISO date binding)\n\n## Inside `addOwner`, in order\n\n3. **`normalizeAddress`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 canonicalizes `address` and writes it back onto the DTO; a `null` address is left untouched (so step 4 still flags it).\n4. **`rejectBlankOwnerFields`** *(validation)* \u2014 rejects (400, `InvalidOwnerFieldsException`) if any of `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` is null or whitespace-only. Closes the gap where Bean Validation permits whitespace-only strings.\n5. **`rejectInvalidPostcode`** *(validation)* \u2014 if a `postcode` is present, it must be valid for the `city` per the region table (Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown city accepts any 4 digits). Rejects 400 otherwise. Absent postcode is accepted.\n6. **`normalizeTelephone`** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 normalizes `telephone` to E.164 and writes it back; rejects 400 if it can't be normalized.\n7. **`normalizeEmail`** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 if `email` is present/non-blank, normalizes (lower-cases) and writes it back; rejects 400 if invalid **or** its domain is on the disposable-domain blocklist. Absent/blank email is skipped.\n8. **`householdIdFor`** *(compute)* \u2014 derives `householdId` from `lastName` + `postcode`.\n9. Reads the `sharesHousehold` opt-in flag (`Boolean.TRUE.equals(...)`).\n10. **`rejectDuplicateIdentity`** *(validation)* \u2014 rejects 409 (`DuplicateOwnerIdentityException`) if any existing owner already has the same normalized telephone (comparison key). *(Note: despite the identity-key naming/docs, the actual match is on telephone alone.)*\n11. **`rejectHouseholdDuplicate`** *(validation)* \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold` is true (or `householdId` is null), rejects 409 (`DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException`) if any existing owner already carries that `householdId`.\n12. **`rejectCityAtCapacity`** *(validation)* \u2014 rejects 409 (`OwnerCityAtCapacityException`) if the `city` (case-insensitive) already holds \u2265 `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY` (50) owners.\n13. **`rejectFutureRegistrationDate`** *(validation)* \u2014 rejects 400 if the *supplied* `registrationDate` is after `LocalDate.now()` (checked before any business-day adjustment).\n14. **`effectiveRegistrationDate`** *(compute)* \u2014 uses the supplied date, or today if null; then rolls Sat/Sun forward to Monday (`BusinessDayAdjuster`).\n15. **`countRegisteredOn`** *(compute)* \u2014 counts existing owners whose stored `registrationDate` equals the effective date.\n16. **`rejectDailyRegistrationLimitReached`** *(validation)* \u2014 rejects 429 (`OwnerDailyRegistrationLimitException`) if that count is \u2265 `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY` (100).\n17. **`ownerMapper.toOwner`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 builds the `Owner` entity from the (now normalized) DTO fields.\n18. **`setRegistrationDate`** \u2014 stamps the effective (business-day-adjusted) registration date.\n19. **`setHouseholdId`** \u2014 stamps the derived household id.\n20. **`setNamesakeCount`** (`countNamesakes`) \u2014 count of existing owners sharing the same first + last name (case-insensitive).\n21. **`setBulkSignupWarning`** \u2014 `true` when `registeredThatDay > BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD` (80).\n22. **`setHouseholdSize`** (`countHouseholdMembers` + 1) \u2014 existing household members plus this one.\n23. **`markPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicateOf` (id of oldest existing owner with same last name + postcode but a different telephone) and `possibleDuplicate` (true when such a match exists). Always cleared to null/false when `sharesHousehold` is true.\n24. **`clinicService.saveOwner`** *(side-effect / persistence)* \u2014 if the owner is new and has no `customerCode`, generates one (`<REGION>-<HASH8>` from postcode-derived region + SHA-256 of telephone+lastName), then persists via the repository (assigning the id).\n25. **Audit log** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `AUDIT` logger emits one line with the new id, customer code, and registration date.\n26. **Response assembly** *(side-effect)* \u2014 maps the saved entity to `OwnerDto` (the mapper derives display-only fields: `displayName`, `initials`, `locality`, `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber`, `membershipPoints`, `membershipLevel`, `contactPreference`, `identityKey`, `ageBand`, `telephoneDisplay`), sets the `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, and returns **201 Created**.\n\n(The V2 controller, `OwnerRestControllerV2`, has no create endpoint \u2014 it only exposes a paged `GET`, so all creation goes through the V1 path above.)"
